Lojbab:
[I had written:]
> >> >Also, it makes sense to say {mi nitcu lo nu broda} if and only
> >> >if it does not make sense to say {mi nitcu lo fasnu}

This is assuming that nu is an event-type, that {lo nu broda cu
fasnu} makes sense and therefore that fasnu means something like
"event-type x1 is instantiated". In this case, what I said is
wrong. Every fasnu is a nu, and {mi nitcu lo fasnu} means "I need
there to be an instance of instantiated event-type x2".

Of course, if "fasnu" means an actual event, then what I oroginally
said was correct, and {lo nu broda cu fasnu} is false.

